{"tool_name":"metaeuk","contents":["biocontainers","galaxy","bioschemas","biotools","bioconda","oeb"],"fetched_metadata":{"bioconda":{"name":"metaeuk","version":"7.bba0d80","home":"https://github.com/soedinglab/metaeuk","license":"GPL-3","summary":"MetaEuk - sensitive, high-throughput gene discovery and annotation for large-scale eukaryotic metagenomics","identifiers":["doi:10.1186/s40168-020-00808-x","biotools:metaeuk"],"license_file":"LICENCE.md","build":{"number":2,"run_exports":[null]},"requirements":{"build":[null,null,"cmake","make","llvm-openmp","libgomp"],"host":["perl","gawk","zlib","bzip2"],"run":["wget","gawk","zlib","bzip2"]},"source_url":"https://github.com/soedinglab/metaeuk/archive/7-bba0d80.tar.gz","test":{"commands":["metaeuk > /dev/null"]},"recipe_maintainers":["milot-mirdita","elileka"]},"biocontainers":{"name":"metaeuk","identifiers":["doi:10.1186/s40168-020-00808-x","doi:10.1101/851964"],"license":"GPL-3","summary":"MetaEuk - sensitive, high-throughput gene discovery and annotation for large-scale eukaryotic metagenomics","home_url":"https://github.com/soedinglab/metaeuk","keywords":["Computational Biology","Databases, Genetic","Eukaryota","High-Throughput Screening Assays","Metagenome","Metagenomics","Microbiota","Molecular Sequence Annotation","Sequence Analysis, DNA","Genomics","Protein Sequences"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":4},"biotools":{"id":"MetaEuk","home":"https://metaeuk.soedinglab.org/","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"MetaEuk - sensitive, high-throughput gene discovery and annotation for large-scale eukaryotic metagenomics","addition_date":"2019-11-29T23:10:08Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T14:34:33.799836Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"version":["1-ea903e5","2-ddf2742"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:MetaEuk","cost":"Free of charge","edit_permission":{"authors":["ELIXIR-CZ"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"cmd":"metaeuk easy-predict input-contigs.fa reference-proteins.fa predictions.fa scratch-dir","input":[{"data":{"term":"Sequence set (nucleic acid)","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1234"},"format":[{"term":"FASTA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1929"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"Homology-based gene prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3663"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Sequence set (protein)","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1233"},"format":[{"term":"FASTA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1929"}]}]}],"maturity":"Emerging","name":"MetaEuk","operating_system":["Linux","Mac"],"owner":"milot-mirdita","publication":[{"doi":"10.1101/851964"},{"doi":"10.1186/s40168-020-00808-x","metadata":{"abstract":"Background: Metagenomics is revolutionizing the study of microorganisms and their involvement in biological, biomedical, and geochemical processes, allowing us to investigate by direct sequencing a tremendous diversity of organisms without the need for prior cultivation. Unicellular eukaryotes play essential roles in most microbial communities as chief predators, decomposers, phototrophs, bacterial hosts, symbionts, and parasites to plants and animals. Investigating their roles is therefore of great interest to ecology, biotechnology, human health, and evolution. However, the generally lower sequencing coverage, their more complex gene and genome architectures, and a lack of eukaryote-specific experimental and computational procedures have kept them on the sidelines of metagenomics. Results: MetaEuk is a toolkit for high-throughput, reference-based discovery, and annotation of protein-coding genes in eukaryotic metagenomic contigs. It performs fast searches with 6-frame-translated fragments covering all possible exons and optimally combines matches into multi-exon proteins. We used a benchmark of seven diverse, annotated genomes to show that MetaEuk is highly sensitive even under conditions of low sequence similarity to the reference database. To demonstrate MetaEuk's power to discover novel eukaryotic proteins in large-scale metagenomic data, we assembled contigs from 912 samples of the Tara Oceans project. MetaEuk predicted >12,000,000 protein-coding genes in 8 days on ten 16-core servers. Most of the discovered proteins are highly diverged from known proteins and originate from very sparsely sampled eukaryotic supergroups. Conclusion: The open-source (GPLv3) MetaEuk software (https://github.com/soedinglab/metaeuk) enables large-scale eukaryotic metagenomics through reference-based, sensitive taxonomic and functional annotation. [MediaObject not available: See fulltext.]","authors":[{"name":"Levy Karin E."},{"name":"Mirdita M."},{"name":"Soding J."}],"citationCount":117,"date":"2020-04-03T00:00:00Z","journal":"Microbiome","title":"MetaEuk-sensitive, high-throughput gene discovery, and annotation for large-scale eukaryotic metagenomics"},"pmcid":"PMC7126354","pmid":"32245390"}],"topic":[{"term":"Gene and protein families","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0623"},{"term":"Metagenomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3174"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"MetaEuk","home":"https://bio.tools/MetaEuk","license":"GPL-3.0","version":["1-ea903e5","2-ddf2742"],"summary":"MetaEuk - sensitive, high-throughput gene discovery and annotation for large-scale eukaryotic metagenomics","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"galaxy":{"version":"@TOOL_VERSION@","first_commit":"2020-08-04","conda_name":"metaeuk","conda_version":"6.a5d39d9","summary":"MetaEuk is a modular toolkit designed for large-scale gene discovery andannotation in eukaryotic metagenomic contigs. Metaeuk combines the fast andsensitive homology search capabilities of MMseqs2 with a dynamic programmingprocedure to recover optimal exons sets. It reduces redundancies in multiplediscoveries of the same gene and resolves conflicting gene predictions onthe same strand. ","edam_operations":["Homology-based gene prediction"],"edam_topics":["Metagenomics","Gene and protein families"],"toolshed_categories":["Sequence Analysis","Genome an